1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,110
The forthcoming "Promised Day".

22
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:41,370
People are continuing to prepare for the day that will determine their fate.

23
00:01:42,990 --> 00:01:47,040
Time passes by, and it is now spring.

24
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:50,290
At last, the Promised Day is about to arrive.

25
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:54,020
Looming Shadows

26
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:54,020
Looming Shadows

27
00:01:59,130 --> 00:02:00,720
Some sort of festival?

28
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:04,100
It's the Festival of the Sheep, a local specialty of Resembool that takes place every spring.

29
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:08,850
Sorry to ask something like this on an important day, but we'd like to replenish our water supplies.

30
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:09,890
Sure thing.

31
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:11,270
Have all the water you want.

32
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,440
Okay! Bring out the water tanks!

33
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,110
One, two...

34
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:19,820
There.

35
00:02:38,130 --> 00:02:39,800
Looks like there's no one home.

36
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:42,140
Here we are, miss.

37
00:02:58,070 --> 00:02:59,530
Home sweet home.

38
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:08,330
Wow, this place is full of automails.

39
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,450
Please don't touch the ones that aren't finished yet.

40
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:24,970
It's so dusty in here...

41
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:41,280
What happened?!

42
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:44,570
Edward Elric?!

43
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,240
Intruders?!

44
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,290
Oww!!

45
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,790
What the hell are you guys doing?

46
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:53,960
Lin?!

47
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:57,170
If I recall, you two are working for Kimblee!

48
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:57,790
Huh?

49
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:01,670
You guys are... from Briggs!

50
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:04,130
You chased us all the way down here?!

51
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:06,930
Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait!

52
00:04:06,930 --> 00:04:07,680
Put down your guns!

53
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:11,180
Hey Ed... just what  is going on?

54
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:13,850
Long story.

55
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:16,440
Besides, what were you doing in my room?!

56
00:04:16,730 --> 00:04:19,610
I just wanted to eat while enjoying the outside view every once in a while!

57
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:21,780
I said, put down your gun!

58
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,240
Quit yelling!

59
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,610
This dog is so loud.

60
00:04:27,110 --> 00:04:29,660
Get the hell out of my room!!

61
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,300
You had me worried sick.

62
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:45,010
I know.

63
00:04:45,010 --> 00:04:47,130
Glad to see you're safe.

64
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:49,100
A-Al isn't with you?

65
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,060
Al's at the station!

66
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,600
He's with Major Miles.

67
00:04:56,310 --> 00:04:57,770
But they're about to depart soon.

68
00:04:57,770 --> 00:04:59,610
If you hurry, you may be able to make it in time.

69
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:06,950
Something wrong?

70
00:05:07,570 --> 00:05:08,660
Aren't you going to go see him?

71
00:05:11,490 --> 00:05:13,950
We're fugitives wanted by Central.

72
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,250
It would be bad if someone were to see us.

73
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:19,420
But...

74
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:33,260
The Festival of the Sheep, huh...

75
00:05:33,850 --> 00:05:35,310
Sure brings back memories.

76
00:05:37,690 --> 00:05:39,100
We're going to be departing soon.

77
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:40,440
Roger.

78
00:05:44,030 --> 00:05:48,950
I hope you will have found your body by the next time you return to this town.

79
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:51,030
Thank you.

80
00:06:06,710 --> 00:06:07,880
Winry?

81
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:14,470
Welcome home.

82
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:16,220
Thanks.

83
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:19,060
Sorry for worrying you.

84
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:24,110
Looks like we have more of you dowdy people in here now.

85
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:26,530
Sorry for causing such a ruckus earlier.

86
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:29,570
We're soldiers from Briggs.

87
00:06:29,570 --> 00:06:32,280
We were dispatched as Miss Winry's bodyguards.

88
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:35,950
You're Lin... right?

89
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:36,990
What?

90
00:06:36,990 --> 00:06:38,950
You know this dude?

91
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:42,920
The name's Greed.

92
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:43,960
Nice to meet ya.

93
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:46,590
Huh?

94
00:06:51,930 --> 00:06:55,600
And so, these guys are currently working for me.

95
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,350
What made you come here?

96
00:06:57,350 --> 00:07:00,770
To make sure his automail's all tuned up and stuff.

97
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:03,230
You know, to prepare for the worst.

98
00:07:03,230 --> 00:07:04,810
Take a look at him later, Winry.

99
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:10,490
You made all his latest stuff, so I can't do the fine-tuning.

100
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:13,990
Sure, no problem.

101
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:19,410
Oh...

102
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,420
So the people of Lior have gotten back up on their feet again.

103
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,580
That's a relief.

104
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:26,040
It's been bugging me, to tell you the truth.

105
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:32,930
So, why is Al with Major Miles?

106
00:07:33,510 --> 00:07:37,970
I heard the people from Briggs are going to do something at the joint exercises in the east.

107
00:07:38,470 --> 00:07:42,180
Al volunteered to join them, saying there might be something he could help out with.

108
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:44,350
Oh...

109
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:49,280
Your dad went to Central ahead of him.

110
00:07:49,650 --> 00:07:54,910
I heard he's in some slum called 'Kanama', so you should meet up with him to get the details.

111
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:02,000
The Promised Day is coming up... right?

112
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:07,750
I heard about that from Greed as well.

113
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:14,800
It's a day when we may be able to get our bodies back,
 or a day when a great tragedy will strike this nation.

114
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:19,140
Hey...

115
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,310
Yeah?

116
00:08:22,770 --> 00:08:25,690
Take Granny and Den and escape to another country.

117
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,650
Are you telling me to run away?!

118
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:31,480
Telling those close to you to escape makes it sound like you've already given up!

119
00:08:32,030 --> 00:08:34,950
Can't you stop the threat to this country?!

120
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:36,570
I'll stop them!

121
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:39,070
But there's a one in a million chance that it may not work!

122
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:41,330
Be 100% sure, then!

123
00:08:42,450 --> 00:08:45,620
They're planning to do something terrible, aren't they?!

124
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:48,330
Beat them to a pulp and protect our country!

125
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:53,300
And while you're at it, get your bodies back and return safe and sound!

126
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,840
I'll do anything  to make that happen!

127
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:04,480
Geez, you make it sound like a walk in the park.

128
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,680
What's this?!

129
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,100
You're not acting like yourself-

130
00:09:08,810 --> 00:09:09,860
Hey, Ed!

131
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:13,690
Gosh, you're such an annoying woman.

132
00:09:13,690 --> 00:09:14,690
Ed!

133
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:25,250
Fine woman you have up there.

134
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:28,500
She just sounds like she wants everything
in the world. Quite the greedy one.

135
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:32,290
When you get too greedy, it comes back to bite you in the behind.

136
00:09:33,050 --> 00:09:33,880
See this?

137
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:36,920
I wanted to bring back the dead, and this was my reward.

138
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:38,260
You really think so?

139
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:44,720
"I long to see someone who died",
"I want to be rich", "I want women"...

140
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,930
"I want to protect the world"...

141
00:09:46,930 --> 00:09:49,020
They're all desires.

142
00:09:49,650 --> 00:09:51,270
In other words, wishes.

143
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:56,110
If you ask me, there's neither 'right' nor 'wrong' when it comes to greed.

144
00:09:57,110 --> 00:10:02,240
You humans go around ranking certain types of greed in order from good to bad, which makes you so hard to understand.

145
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:13,670
You're leaving now  of all times?

146
00:10:13,670 --> 00:10:17,800
We were planning on leaving today anyway.

147
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:22,800
Thanks for the tune-up.

148
00:10:24,930 --> 00:10:29,770
If you ever happen to see Hohenheim, deliver Trisha's message for her.

149
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,730
Sure, whatever.

150
00:10:31,730 --> 00:10:33,270
Ed! I...

151
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:35,730
You stay hidden.

152
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:42,530
I'll come home after putting an end to everything on the Promised Day, so...

153
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:45,280
...wait for us with a freshly-baked apple pie. Deal?

154
00:10:48,330 --> 00:10:49,120
Deal!

155
00:10:59,210 --> 00:11:01,010
Work today took forever.

156
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:04,470
But hey, is this really what we should be focusing on right now?

157
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,640
The Promised Day is coming up!

158
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:08,350
Not much else we can do!

159
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:10,850
Doctor Marcoh and Scar haven't met up with us yet!

160
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,190
Geez... where the hell are they?!

161
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:19,490
Doctor!

162
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:20,940
Hey, it's you guys.

163
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,450
"Hey, it's you guys"?!

164
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:25,450
Where have you two been all this time?!

165
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:27,450
Sorry about that.

166
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:30,330
Let's head over to Central.

167
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:36,540
But something feels a little off.

168
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:41,590
We used to be soldiers, but now we're working with an Ishbalan.

169
00:11:41,590 --> 00:11:42,880
Yeah it does.

170
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:47,100
For us, Amestris is our birthplace.

171
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,560
We've got family here as well.

172
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:56,150
But Scar, who used to rebel against the nation, is now working to protect it.

173
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:57,900
Don't get the wrong idea.

174
00:11:57,900 --> 00:12:00,110
My goal is not to protect this country.

175
00:12:00,110 --> 00:12:01,070
I'm working to change it.

176
00:12:03,450 --> 00:12:06,950
I'm working in order for the people of this country to recognize the existence of the Ishbalans,

177
00:12:06,950 --> 00:12:10,990
a race that they denied.

178
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:16,000
In order to change the world,
you must start by changing yourself.

179
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:20,500
That's how it is, Amestrians.

180
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,050
Ishbalans?!

181
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:22,970
Why?!

182
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:27,760
We weren't just dawdling about for months doing nothing.

183
00:12:29,010 --> 00:12:31,770
They're comrades who share our goal.

184
00:12:46,030 --> 00:12:48,530
May this year's exercises be productive as always, Lieutenant General.

185
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:54,160
I'm glad we're doing it in the east this year.

186
00:12:54,710 --> 00:12:57,620
Joint exercises in the north are pretty tough for us.

187
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:04,550
Everything's ready on our end.

188
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,970
Ours, too.

189
00:13:07,470 --> 00:13:10,600
Unfortunately, a little problem has popped up...

190
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,140
That being?

191
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:20,730
Little miss Bradley is here to observe as well.

192
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:30,490
I was expecting someone high up to watch over the practice, since it's right before the Promised Day...

193
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:34,870
We'll just have to figure something out.

194
00:13:53,970 --> 00:13:55,220
There it is again...

195
00:13:59,690 --> 00:14:03,820
The delay between visions is gradually getting shorter.

196
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,240
I have to hurry.

197
00:14:06,610 --> 00:14:08,780
I need to get my body back, or...

198
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:24,460
Yeah, I can smell him!

199
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:28,010
Smells like the Fullmetal Alchemist's little brother!

200
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,010
Running away?

201
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:34,390
This isn't good!

202
00:14:34,970 --> 00:14:37,520
I'm in no condition to fight!

203
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:58,000
What's... this...?!

204
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,920
Talk about great timing...!

205
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:23,900
I'm going to have you keep quiet until the Promised Day,

206
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:26,480
Alphonse Elric.

207
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:47,630
Good evening, Major General.

208
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:52,590
I've got no tea for the likes of you.

209
00:15:56,850 --> 00:16:00,470
I may be able to take you out for dinner soon.

210
00:16:00,470 --> 00:16:03,270
So you finally plan to fulfill the promise from forever ago?

211
00:16:07,270 --> 00:16:12,280
'Large' doesn't even begin to describe this mansion.
The wealth of the Armstrong family never ceases to amaze me.

212
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:17,280
You could fit a company... no, even a full battalion in here.

213
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,290
If something may happen to me,

214
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,500
you can have the entire mansion.

215
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,750
It won't fit into my coffin, after all.

216
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,130
You're not going to give it to your brother?

217
00:16:34,550 --> 00:16:39,680
I'd say you're the better choice... by a hair.

218
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:42,560
That's quite an honor.

219
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:47,600
Belatedly...

220
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:50,940
This is to congratulate you for becoming the head of the Armstrong family.

221
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,610
Hyacinths...?

222
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:05,000
"Selim Bradley is a Homunculus."

223
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:10,090
Are you aware of what the Hyacinth represents?

224
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:12,960
I'm not.

225
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,380
Feminine beauty.

226
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:20,100
I don't need your flowers!

227
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:25,180
Well, if you'll excuse me, Major General.

228
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:30,150
You amateur.

229
00:17:37,990 --> 00:17:41,720
One Day Prior to the "Promised Day"

230
00:17:37,990 --> 00:17:41,700
One Day Prior to the "Promised Day"

231
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:53,210
This is annoying.

232
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:58,340
We should just aim a cannon at Bradley's tower and be done with it.

233
00:17:58,340 --> 00:17:59,590
Please don't.

234
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:00,930
Major Miles.

235
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:06,430
So we still don't have a clue as to where Alphonse Elric disappeared to...

236
00:18:06,430 --> 00:18:09,600
Yes. We're still searching, but...

237
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:12,610
Could it be that he was captured?

238
00:18:15,110 --> 00:18:17,690
And the Promised Day is tomorrow...

239
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:20,700
Sire.

240
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:23,740
Major General Hakuro has arrived.

241
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:28,710
Sire, there's something I need to inform you about Lieutenant General Grumman-

242
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:31,250
A coup d'etat using the Eastern army?

243
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:34,250
We've already planned for such eventualities.

244
00:18:34,670 --> 00:18:38,760
No, the joint practice is a bait.

245
00:18:39,510 --> 00:18:43,510
The Ishbalan remnants will commit a terrorist act in Central,

246
00:18:43,510 --> 00:18:45,760
now that defenses have weakened since Your Highness is here in the east.

247
00:18:47,390 --> 00:18:52,230
Lieutenant General Grumman will use "terrorist suppression" as a pretense to invade Central.

248
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:55,770
He's planning on taking advantage of the confusion to take over Central Headquarters,

249
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,400
with the help of Colonel Mustang.

250
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,960
Just as Major General Hakuro stated,

251
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:16,250
many Ishbalans have infiltrated Central vicinity over the past few days.

252
00:19:25,550 --> 00:19:27,720
I'm returning to Central.

253
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,140
I'll leave matters here in your hands.

254
00:19:29,430 --> 00:19:30,310
Roger.

255
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:39,440
That damned Mustang... planning something outrageous.

256
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:43,990
I thought we took care of him when we
separated him from all of his useful men...

257
00:19:55,750 --> 00:19:56,750
The train stopped.

258
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,500
What's going on?

259
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:02,920
Sheep crossing.

260
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,840
Dammit, we're in a rush for time...!

261
00:20:12,390 --> 00:20:15,400
Hey, they just left us!

262
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,270
What?!

263
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,520
What's going on?!

264
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:19,270
Hey! Make him stop!

265
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:40,130
The sheep on the tracks have been exterminated.

266
00:20:40,130 --> 00:20:42,710
We'll be heading to Central as planned.

267
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:44,930
Let's go!

268
00:20:44,930 --> 00:20:46,220
The Colonel is awaiting our arrival.

269
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:47,390
Yes, sir!

270
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:48,760
Dammit!

271
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:55,230
You played right into their hands, Major General Hakuro.

272
00:20:57,060 --> 00:21:00,570
The train that was carrying the Führer President has been bombed!

273
00:21:00,730 --> 00:21:01,440
What?!

274
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:18,120
Everything begins tomorrow.

275
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,830
Time to make our move,

276
00:21:20,290 --> 00:21:22,340
Second Lieutenant Breda, Master Sergeant Fuery.

277
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:24,760
No need for the "Second Lieutenant", ma'am.

278
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:27,260
We're just plain old deserters now.

279
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:29,930
There goes my future...

280
00:21:31,510 --> 00:21:35,520
We'll have the Colonel take responsibility after everything's over.

281
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:58,290
The promise we never made

282
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:58,290
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

283
00:21:58,290 --> 00:21:59,080
yet again

284
00:21:58,290 --> 00:21:59,080
Kyou mo

285
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:03,920
tries to snatch our future away from us.

286
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:03,920
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

287
00:22:05,550 --> 00:22:09,510
Why is it that we can't rejoice

288
00:22:05,550 --> 00:22:09,510
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

289
00:22:09,510 --> 00:22:10,510
straight from the heart

290
00:22:09,510 --> 00:22:10,510
Sunao ni

291
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:15,470
when we obtain something we've always been after?

292
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:15,470
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

293
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:21,190
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

294
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:21,190
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

295
00:22:21,860 --> 00:22:25,980
They're fragments born from agony.

296
00:22:21,860 --> 00:22:25,980
Itami ga unda kakera de

297
00:22:27,650 --> 00:22:31,030
Of all the moments and destinies,

298
00:22:27,650 --> 00:22:31,030
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

299
00:22:31,030 --> 00:22:39,790
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

300
00:22:31,030 --> 00:22:39,790
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

301
00:22:39,790 --> 00:22:42,330
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

302
00:22:39,790 --> 00:22:42,330
Genkai datte konnan datte

303
00:22:42,330 --> 00:22:46,340
I refuse to give up.

304
00:22:42,330 --> 00:22:46,340
Akirametakunaiyo

305
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:51,220
Please, don't let go.

306
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:51,220
Konomama hanasanaide

307
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:59,060
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

308
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:59,060
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

309
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:02,730
where it's tightly joined with my left.

310
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:02,730
Koko ni arukara

311
00:23:10,780 --> 00:23:12,070
The Führer President?!

312
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:14,530
There's no way King Bradley could die...!

313
00:23:14,910 --> 00:23:17,200
We can't make assumptions just yet!

314
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,790
What has the investigation turned up?!

315
00:23:18,790 --> 00:23:20,660
The squadron has yet to reach the scene of the accident!

316
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:23,120
As soon as their leader is gone, this happens.

317
00:23:20,910 --> 00:23:22,080
Make them hurry up!

318
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,120
Quit yelling!

319
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:23,630
PLACEHOLDER

320
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:24,750
This is not my job!

321
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:25,790
In the end, they're nothing but an undisciplined mob.

322
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:25,590
But...!

323
00:23:25,590 --> 00:23:27,960
This isn't the time for this!

324
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:31,300
PLACEHOLDER

325
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:30,260
The supreme commander is missing!

326
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:31,420
I know that!

327
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:32,970
This may be my chance...

328
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:42,020
I never expected someone as important as you to visit this place.

329
00:23:43,270 --> 00:23:45,560
Calm down, everyone.

330
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:54,280
I'm still here.

331
00:23:59,620 --> 00:24:01,250
What lurks in the shadows?

332
00:24:01,580 --> 00:24:04,960
Demons? Beasts? Monsters?

333
00:24:05,750 --> 00:24:11,210
A black gust of wind saves our heroes who are faced with a crisis.

334
00:24:12,420 --> 00:24:16,720
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

335
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:20,750
Episode 47, Emissary of Darkness.

336
00:24:16,740 --> 00:24:20,750
Emissary of Darkness

337
00:24:21,310 --> 00:24:26,310
Shed light on the heart of man. To an engulfing darkness.
